      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: While you are touching this code, it appears that the rounding logic here is broken and has never worked correctly.\n\n`LIS2DW12_NORMALIZE_FS(fs)` is defined as `(1 \u003c\u003c (30 - __builtin_clz(_fs)))`. For `newrange` values 2, 4, 8, 16 it evaluates to 1, 2, 4, 8 respectively.\nSince `newrange` is always strictly greater than `newrange / 2`, the condition `newrange \u003c LIS2DW12_NORMALIZE_FS(newrange)` will always evaluate to false for any valid clamped range.\nAs a result, `newrange \u003c\u003c\u003d 1` never executes and the driver fails to round up to the next full scale range when `rnd` is set.\n\nYou might want to fix this (either in this patch or a follow-up) by fixing `LIS2DW12_NORMALIZE_FS` and changing the logic to:\n```c\n\tint normalized \u003d LIS2DW12_NORMALIZE_FS(newrange);\n\n\t/* Adjust and check rounded value. */\n\tif (rnd \u0026\u0026 (normalized \u003c range))\n\t\tnormalized \u003c\u003c\u003d 1;\n\t\n\tnewrange \u003d normalized;\n```\n(The clamp added in this patch is perfectly correct and successfully fixes the undefined behavior and division by zero issues).",
